cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it with the metadata below. The accompanying manuscript is unpublished and has not been peer reviewed."
title: "MARS-NLP: Robust Multilingual Scam Message Classification with Character-Level and Transformer-Based NLP"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rizwan"
    given-names: "Muhammad"
    email: "rizwan01107@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >-
  Binary scam message classification for English, Roman Urdu and code-switched SMS text. Character- and word-level TF-IDF
  classifiers are compared with fine-tuned mBERT and XLM-R under group-aware (near-duplicate) splitting, with a synthetic
  perturbation suite and cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals.
keywords:
  - scam message detection
  - Roman Urdu
  - code-switching
  - multilingual transformers
  - robustness
